# Size measurement only (owner, 2026-11-09): what BTF and the function tracers
# add to the station's boot image now that the RAM root is xz-compressed. Not
# booted. BTF needs DWARF at build time; pahole turns it into the .BTF section,
# and modules get their own. The kernel headers archive is a module, so it stays
# out of boot2 until it is loaded. arm64's defconfig reduces the debug info, which
# BTF cannot use.
#
# Result (ce66951a against D3's 5ed802b4, both composed from the same parent RAM
# root and tools, modules stripped of DWARF with BTF kept):
# - Image.gz 8,625,642 -> 10,724,764 bytes (+2.10 MB). The kernel's .BTF section
#   is 5.51 MB before compression, the mcount table 0.35 MB, text +0.5 MB.
# - The xz RAM root 4,068,808 -> 4,346,488 bytes (+0.28 MB): the modules' BTF.
# - boot.img 12,744,704 -> 15,122,432 bytes (+2.38 MB), 1.58 MiB under boot2's
#   16 MiB. It fits, but only with the modules stripped: unstripped they are
#   265 MB instead of 29 MB, so a booted profile also needs INSTALL_MOD_STRIP.
# CONFIG_DEBUG_INFO_NONE is not set
CONFIG_DEBUG_INFO_DWARF_TOOLCHAIN_DEFAULT=y
# CONFIG_DEBUG_INFO_REDUCED is not set
CONFIG_DEBUG_INFO_BTF=y
CONFIG_DEBUG_INFO_BTF_MODULES=y
CONFIG_FUNCTION_TRACER=y
CONFIG_DYNAMIC_FTRACE=y
CONFIG_IKHEADERS=m
